    "scientific_justification": "MEmagenta is the strongest module-level stage association (r = +0.4804, P = 0.00466; 37 genes) and contains zero upregulated ECM DEGs. MEblack contains 2,398 genes and 25 upregulated ECM DEGs, but its eigengene is not associated with stage (r = +0.0285, P = 0.8748). All seven majority hubs are assigned to black, yet their calculated kME_black correlations are weak and nonsignificant while their individual stage gene-significance correlations are positive. Thus, neither module is fully supported as a unified immune-matrisome hub cluster: the current files support a distinct MEmagenta module-trait association and individual hub-stage associations, but do not establish black-module co-expression or the claimed WGCNA-convergent provenance."
